AWS Static Website with Terraform

This project demonstrates how to deploy a static website on AWS using Terraform as Infrastructure as Code (IaC). The goal is to automate the creation and configuration of the required cloud resources so a website can be hosted directly from an Amazon S3 bucket.
The Terraform configuration creates an S3 bucket and enables static website hosting on it. The bucket is configured with an index document so that when users access the website URL, the main HTML file is automatically served as the default page.
